WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.628 --> 00:00:03.141
- What are you most proud
of in your playing career?

00:00:03.141 --> 00:00:05.957
- I'm most proud of my
outstanding free-throw percentage.

00:00:05.957 --> 00:00:08.542
(audience laughing)

00:00:08.542 --> 00:00:10.916
51%, make one, miss one.

00:00:10.916 --> 00:00:13.158
One day, you're going to be recognized.

00:00:13.158 --> 00:00:15.437
Your name will be remembered
because you are different.

00:00:15.437 --> 00:00:17.052
So master being different.

00:00:17.052 --> 00:00:18.908
You know, my mother always told me,

00:00:18.908 --> 00:00:21.812
Make 'em remember your name.

00:00:21.812 --> 00:00:25.594
No matter how, make
'em remember your name.

00:00:25.594 --> 00:00:28.031
He's a retired professional
basketball player.

00:00:28.031 --> 00:00:29.767
He was drafted by the Orlando Magic

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:32.991
and quickly became one of
the best centers in the NBA.

00:00:32.991 --> 00:00:35.198
He's currently an
analyst on the TV program

00:00:35.198 --> 00:00:37.199
Inside the NBA.

00:00:37.199 --> 00:00:38.231
He's Shaquille O'Neal

00:00:38.231 --> 00:00:41.015
and here's my take on his
top 10 rules for success.

00:00:41.015 --> 00:00:42.799
Rule number one is my personal favorite,

00:00:42.799 --> 00:00:45.014
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:45.014 --> 00:00:46.998
And always as you're watching,
if you hear something

00:00:46.998 --> 00:00:48.675
that really resonates with you,

00:00:48.675 --> 00:00:50.326
please leave it in the comments below,

00:00:50.326 --> 00:00:51.591
put quotes around it so other people

00:00:51.591 --> 00:00:53.151
can be inspired as well,

00:00:53.151 --> 00:00:55.111
and when you write it
down, it's much more likely

00:00:55.111 --> 00:00:57.861
to stick with you as well, enjoy.

00:01:01.111 --> 00:01:03.694
(upbeat music)

00:01:11.295 --> 00:01:13.846
- What is it about investment
and entrepreneurship

00:01:13.846 --> 00:01:16.591
that sort of has bitten you?

00:01:16.591 --> 00:01:19.791
- I never look at it as
investments, believe it or not.

00:01:19.791 --> 00:01:22.982
I just look at it as partnerships.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.743
I help changing the world.

00:01:24.743 --> 00:01:28.014
And just being part of
something that's inspiring.

00:01:28.014 --> 00:01:29.311
My business people, all the time,

00:01:29.311 --> 00:01:31.906
whenever they talk about money,
you got to ask 'em about yaa,

00:01:31.906 --> 00:01:32.906
I don't want to hear it.

00:01:32.906 --> 00:01:35.446
But if they bring an idea to me

00:01:35.446 --> 00:01:37.403
that I think is going
to go to the next level,

00:01:37.403 --> 00:01:40.026
most of the time if I follow my heart,

00:01:40.026 --> 00:01:41.507
then everything else will fall in place.

00:01:41.507 --> 00:01:43.210
I've never, ever done a deal,

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:44.962
eh, we've got this suit company,

00:01:44.962 --> 00:01:46.659
we throw some pinstripes in the suit,

00:01:46.659 --> 00:01:49.595
you give me 100,000 we
sell 20 of them we make."

00:01:49.595 --> 00:01:52.075
I've never did a deal where
it was always based on money.

00:01:52.075 --> 00:01:53.930
I've always done my
business deals based on

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:56.138
how I felt it was going
to go in the future,

00:01:56.138 --> 00:02:00.305
how I felt it was going to
help and inspire somebody.

00:02:01.338 --> 00:02:03.331
- [Sportscaster] Mack tries to be trippy,

00:02:03.331 --> 00:02:07.122
and it may cost the
Nuggets a four point swing.

00:02:07.122 --> 00:02:09.587
- [Commentator] You ever
see a man that big fly?

00:02:09.587 --> 00:02:11.978
- What are you most proud
of in your playing career?

00:02:11.978 --> 00:02:14.755
- I'm most proud of my
outstanding free-throw percentage.

00:02:14.755 --> 00:02:17.410
(audience laughing)

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:19.827
51%, make one, miss one.

00:02:24.036 --> 00:02:26.536
I'm most proud that I made it.

00:02:27.817 --> 00:02:31.126
To just fulfill the
dreams and just work hard

00:02:31.126 --> 00:02:34.293
and just persevere through everything.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:40.270
I learned at age 13, 14, 15 to
use criticism as motivation.

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:41.934
So whenever somebody
told me I couldn't do it,

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:45.184
it just made me go out and work harder.

00:02:47.234 --> 00:02:49.462
- [Sportscaster] Orlando
defense is so strong.

00:02:49.462 --> 00:02:52.212
(crowd cheering)

00:02:53.487 --> 00:02:55.664
When you try for the slot,

00:02:55.664 --> 00:02:58.270
you got to maintain body contact,

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:01.862
He fields, he grabs, but he
doesn't move back enough,

00:03:01.862 --> 00:03:03.118
and he gets dunked on.

00:03:03.118 --> 00:03:04.519
How embarrassing is that?

00:03:04.519 --> 00:03:08.090
- Investments not going to always
go how you want them to go.

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:11.061
Business plans not going to
go how you want them to go.

00:03:11.061 --> 00:03:13.394
So you just have to regroup.

00:03:14.757 --> 00:03:16.160
- [Interviewer] You say
regroup, what does that mean?

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:16.993
What does that look like?

00:03:16.993 --> 00:03:18.933
- Okay, my theory, my
thought process is to

00:03:18.933 --> 00:03:22.558
never focus on the problem,
focus on the solution.

00:03:22.558 --> 00:03:23.958
I invested in this water company,

00:03:23.958 --> 00:03:26.773
it didn't go well, that money's gone.

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:29.878
Now I got to regroup, now
I got to do something else.

00:03:29.878 --> 00:03:31.798
So, I'll be upset for about 20 minutes.

00:03:31.798 --> 00:03:35.062
Go to that cabinet, get
them Frosted Flakes.

00:03:35.062 --> 00:03:37.265
Get some of that cold milk.

00:03:37.265 --> 00:03:39.433
Slice them bananas up.

00:03:39.433 --> 00:03:43.010
Watch some ESPN, and then the
next day I'm back on track.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:46.093
- You all got that, that's pretty good.

00:03:47.105 --> 00:03:48.657
But the key thing you said,

00:03:48.657 --> 00:03:51.673
focus on the solution, not on the problem

00:03:51.673 --> 00:03:53.649
because where your energy goes

00:03:53.649 --> 00:03:57.337
that's where your focus
and concentration goes.

00:03:57.337 --> 00:04:00.170
(crowd shouting)

00:04:03.425 --> 00:04:05.675
- [Sportscaster] Whoa baby!

00:04:07.433 --> 00:04:09.049
They're done the rest.

00:04:09.049 --> 00:04:12.396
Alonzo Mourning just got posterized.

00:04:12.396 --> 00:04:16.818
Oh my goodness, he went
flying through the air.

00:04:16.818 --> 00:04:19.697
And he's saying, bang your head.

00:04:19.697 --> 00:04:22.857
- Now one thing I try
to do when I came in was

00:04:22.857 --> 00:04:25.041
I wanted to be different.

00:04:25.041 --> 00:04:27.681
You know, my dad, growing up, I realized

00:04:27.681 --> 00:04:29.321
that I was a little bit different

00:04:29.321 --> 00:04:31.432
but I didn't like being different.

00:04:31.432 --> 00:04:33.352
And he would tell me, "You know what?

00:04:33.352 --> 00:04:36.000
"One day you're going to be recognized.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.465
"Your name will be remembered
because you are different."

00:04:38.465 --> 00:04:40.233
So master being different.

00:04:40.233 --> 00:04:41.169
Don't be like everybody else.

00:04:41.169 --> 00:04:43.086
Master being different.

00:04:44.798 --> 00:04:46.393
- [Sportscaster] Rice falling away.

00:04:46.393 --> 00:04:48.024
Won't go on the rebound.

00:04:48.024 --> 00:04:50.553
Now the Magic with a final shot chance.

00:04:50.553 --> 00:04:52.169
O'Neal runs the court,

00:04:52.169 --> 00:04:53.416
takes it all the way!

00:04:53.416 --> 00:04:56.473
(crowd shouting)

00:04:56.473 --> 00:04:57.798
- [Commentator] Well, that's
ruined my theory there

00:04:57.798 --> 00:05:00.985
because the heat came down and
threw up another free shot.

00:05:00.985 --> 00:05:02.425
- Don't do it because you're trying

00:05:02.425 --> 00:05:04.257
to get your followers up.

00:05:04.257 --> 00:05:05.232
You know what I mean?

00:05:05.232 --> 00:05:07.089
Like, if you're not really with the cause

00:05:07.089 --> 00:05:10.594
and you're not going to
dedicate yourself 1000 percent,

00:05:10.594 --> 00:05:11.504
don't do it.

00:05:11.504 --> 00:05:13.681
Like when you talk about
Jim Brown and Bill Russell

00:05:13.681 --> 00:05:17.056
and those guys, they dedicated
themselves 1000 percent.

00:05:17.056 --> 00:05:19.768
We didn't have Twitter back
then and followers and all that,

00:05:19.768 --> 00:05:21.769
they dedicated themselves 1000 percent.

00:05:21.769 --> 00:05:24.353
So, if you're not going to
dedicate yourself 1000 percent,

00:05:24.353 --> 00:05:27.397
and if you're not going to do
it when the cameras are off,

00:05:27.397 --> 00:05:28.397
don't do it.

00:05:30.008 --> 00:05:32.758
(crowd shouting)

00:05:36.689 --> 00:05:37.681
- [Sportscaster] Oh my goodness!

00:05:37.681 --> 00:05:39.833
Shaquille O'Neal, what an athlete!

00:05:39.833 --> 00:05:41.416
Are you kidding me!

00:05:43.504 --> 00:05:46.032
- David Robinson was the nicest man ever.

00:05:46.032 --> 00:05:49.264
I was a big man on campus in San Antonio

00:05:49.264 --> 00:05:51.432
and then the Spurs, they draft him,

00:05:51.432 --> 00:05:53.169
and he steals all my shine.

00:05:53.169 --> 00:05:54.403
So, I meet him one day and I was like,

00:05:54.403 --> 00:05:56.640
"Mr. Robinson, can I have your autograph?"

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:57.657
'Cause I learned a lot from him.

00:05:57.657 --> 00:06:00.104
I learned as a big man,
you can get easy buckets

00:06:00.104 --> 00:06:01.408
by running the floor.

00:06:01.408 --> 00:06:03.568
I also learned the spin lob thing.

00:06:03.568 --> 00:06:05.856
- [Sportscaster] The old slam through.

00:06:05.856 --> 00:06:07.192
- [Commentator] O'Neal into the lane.

00:06:07.192 --> 00:06:09.136
- [Sportscaster] Slammer, oh baby!

00:06:09.136 --> 00:06:11.024
Save the women and children on that one.

00:06:11.024 --> 00:06:12.376
- I learned that from
watching David Robinson.

00:06:12.376 --> 00:06:13.488
So I meet him.

00:06:13.488 --> 00:06:14.408
We have a conversation.

00:06:14.408 --> 00:06:15.708
He signs my autograph.

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:18.976
First time we plays
the Spurs, he kills me.

00:06:18.976 --> 00:06:21.352
And my father ripped me a new one.

00:06:21.352 --> 00:06:23.067
"You show him too much respect.

00:06:23.067 --> 00:06:24.312
"I don't care if that's David Robinson.

00:06:24.312 --> 00:06:26.240
"You Shaq O'Neal, you need to dominate.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:28.268
"You need to go home and think
about what you need to do."

00:06:28.268 --> 00:06:30.288
So, I was like you know what,

00:06:30.288 --> 00:06:33.568
he didn't give me his autograph
when I was 15 years old.

00:06:33.568 --> 00:06:34.968
That pisses me off.

00:06:34.968 --> 00:06:37.720
From that point on, when
I said that to myself,

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:38.868
that he didn't give me an autograph,

00:06:38.868 --> 00:06:40.824
that he stiffed me for an
autograph as a youngster,

00:06:40.824 --> 00:06:41.992
I wanted to pay him back.

00:06:41.992 --> 00:06:45.435
That was my way of competing
with David Robinson.

00:06:45.435 --> 00:06:46.803
(crowd cheering)

00:06:46.803 --> 00:06:49.720
- [Sportscaster] The lumbering, oh!

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:53.027
Shaq spins, totally!

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:55.944
- [Man] Let me see you miss.

00:06:55.944 --> 00:06:58.694
(glass crashing)

00:07:00.576 --> 00:07:01.409
You all right?

00:07:01.409 --> 00:07:02.704
- [Shaq] Yeah, I'm all right.

00:07:02.704 --> 00:07:05.067
- So, I guess we will never know,

00:07:05.067 --> 00:07:06.128
between the two of us,

00:07:06.128 --> 00:07:09.592
seeing that you just destroyed the basket.

00:07:09.592 --> 00:07:11.808
- [Sportscaster] Last game,
Dennis, Scott was starting.

00:07:11.808 --> 00:07:14.391
Bowie was coming off the bench.

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:18.903
Head's up, bring down
the entire backboard.

00:07:22.568 --> 00:07:23.401
Shaquille.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.208
- [Commentator] I've never seen that.

00:07:28.208 --> 00:07:30.344
- [Sportscaster] Hold on to the roof.

00:07:30.344 --> 00:07:31.677
The Shaq attack.

00:07:33.552 --> 00:07:34.496
- Do you have any advice for people

00:07:34.496 --> 00:07:38.817
looking to branch out
of their comfort zone?

00:07:38.817 --> 00:07:41.567
- You have to value partnerships.

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:46.391
Like I've always been a basketball player.

00:07:46.391 --> 00:07:48.080
I've always played basketball.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:52.168
I could probably say I'm
a master of basketball.

00:07:52.168 --> 00:07:54.806
So, now when I wanted
to become a businessman,

00:07:54.806 --> 00:07:57.712
like I had to go through the
dos and donts of business,

00:07:57.712 --> 00:07:59.152
but to get respect as a businessman

00:07:59.152 --> 00:08:01.103
I was like, "Let me go ahead, get this

00:08:01.103 --> 00:08:02.640
Masters in Business Administration,

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:05.585
so they know and understand
what I'm talking about."

00:08:05.585 --> 00:08:07.736
I've always considered myself a leader.

00:08:07.736 --> 00:08:10.111
So, my thought process is,
let me get this Doctorate

00:08:10.111 --> 00:08:12.559
in leadership so people
would know and understand

00:08:12.559 --> 00:08:15.336
that my thought process
on how I do things.

00:08:15.336 --> 00:08:17.936
But, I've always been
smart enough to have people

00:08:17.936 --> 00:08:20.095
better than me on my team.

00:08:20.095 --> 00:08:21.975
For example, what's the name of this?

00:08:21.975 --> 00:08:22.952
- Tech Crunch.
- Tech Crunch.

00:08:22.952 --> 00:08:25.280
So if I'm going to start a magazine,

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:26.484
So if I'm going to start a magazine,

00:08:26.484 --> 00:08:29.192
called Tech Crunch, you best
believe I'm going to have

00:08:29.192 --> 00:08:32.292
the techiest publisher, I'm going to have

00:08:32.292 --> 00:08:34.008
the techiest camera
guys, I'm going to have

00:08:34.008 --> 00:08:36.392
the techiest interviewers working for me

00:08:36.392 --> 00:08:38.239
rather than me trying to
do everything by myself.

00:08:38.239 --> 00:08:40.800
So, you have to value partnerships.

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:42.224
For example, if I wanted
to be the best Sheriff

00:08:42.224 --> 00:08:45.055
in Austin, Texas, I got to
get the best police officers.

00:08:45.055 --> 00:08:48.880
I can't be the best without
having the best team.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:52.423
So, I've always, always
valued partnerships.

00:08:52.423 --> 00:08:54.552
And I always have people better than me

00:08:54.552 --> 00:08:56.103
and smarter than me around me

00:08:56.103 --> 00:08:59.792
so they can motivate
me, so they can help me.

00:08:59.792 --> 00:09:03.272
(crowd shouting)

00:09:03.272 --> 00:09:05.176
- [Sportscaster] Shaq sends
it back with a blocked shot.

00:09:05.176 --> 00:09:06.343
Here's Shorty.

00:09:08.903 --> 00:09:09.752
Look out below!

00:09:09.752 --> 00:09:13.328
(crowd shouting)

00:09:13.328 --> 00:09:15.295
- [Lady] Wow, that's you?

00:09:15.295 --> 00:09:16.128
- [Shaq] Yes.

00:09:16.128 --> 00:09:16.961
- [Lady] How old were you?

00:09:16.961 --> 00:09:18.752
- [Shaq] 16.

00:09:18.752 --> 00:09:20.287
- [Announcer] Growing up a military brat,

00:09:20.287 --> 00:09:23.320
he frequently changed schools
and had to make new friends.

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:26.352
He struggled to feel
comfortable in his own skin.

00:09:26.352 --> 00:09:29.921
- I've always thrived on uniqueness.

00:09:29.921 --> 00:09:31.480
You know, my mother always told me,

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:32.792
"Make 'em remember your name."

00:09:32.792 --> 00:09:34.743
- [Sportscaster] Oh, oh!

00:09:34.743 --> 00:09:36.719
- "No matter how, make
'em remember your name."

00:09:36.719 --> 00:09:38.939
- [Sportscaster] I can't
believe it, are you serious?

00:09:38.939 --> 00:09:40.968
- [Announcer] Well, I guess
it pays to listen to mom.

00:09:40.968 --> 00:09:42.543
(crowd shouting)

00:09:42.543 --> 00:09:45.210
- [Sportscaster] O'Neal, O'Neal.

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:50.735
Shaq over to Skiles, puts up a three.

00:09:50.735 --> 00:09:54.791
He missed it and Turner chases it down.

00:09:54.791 --> 00:09:57.958
Shaq for two over Olajuwon, whoa baby!

00:09:59.312 --> 00:10:00.562
That was nasty!

00:10:02.791 --> 00:10:03.791
My goodness.

00:10:04.644 --> 00:10:07.092
- I don't want to be
remembered as an athlete

00:10:07.092 --> 00:10:09.508
who made a lot of money, or an athlete

00:10:09.508 --> 00:10:10.548
who did great movies,

00:10:10.548 --> 00:10:13.881
like Kazaam (laughing),

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:17.916
I don't want blue chips,

00:10:17.916 --> 00:10:19.628
I don't want to be remembered

00:10:19.628 --> 00:10:21.660
for a guy that's won a
lot of championships,

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:23.428
I want to be remembered as a guy

00:10:23.428 --> 00:10:26.789
because of his action, he
inspired people to learn more,

00:10:26.789 --> 00:10:29.439
to do more and to want more.

00:10:29.439 --> 00:10:32.606
(audience applauding)

00:10:34.357 --> 00:10:37.469
(crowd shouting)

00:10:37.469 --> 00:10:39.116
- [Sportscaster] Gruli for O'Neal,

00:10:39.116 --> 00:10:40.533
That's a mad jam!

00:10:45.157 --> 00:10:48.157
(audience shouting)

00:12:40.811 --> 00:12:42.419
- [Sportscaster] O'Neal's
going to have to get back

00:12:42.419 --> 00:12:43.798
to the transition spot.

00:12:43.798 --> 00:12:45.268
Oh, what a dunk!

00:12:45.268 --> 00:12:46.764
Hey, look at him look back at Mourning.

00:12:46.764 --> 00:12:49.597
Oh, he came flyin' out of nowhere!

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:56.691
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:12:56.691 --> 00:12:59.723
I made this video because
Phillip Doblosky asked me to.

