00:13:20.555 --> 00:13:22.083
I'm super curious to find out.

00:13:22.083 --> 00:13:23.786
I also want to give a
quick shout out to to Jude.

00:13:23.786 --> 00:13:24.827
Jude, thank you so much

00:13:24.827 --> 00:13:27.051
for picking up a copy
of my book Your One Word

00:13:27.051 --> 00:13:28.435
and taking that picture.

00:13:28.435 --> 00:13:30.907
It's amazing to see,
thank you so much again.

00:13:30.907 --> 00:13:32.035
I appreciate the support,

00:13:32.035 --> 00:13:33.334
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:13:33.334 --> 00:13:35.155
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:13:35.155 --> 00:13:36.595
I believe in you.

00:13:36.595 --> 00:13:38.611
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:13:38.611 --> 00:13:40.691
And whatever your one word is,

00:13:40.691 --> 00:13:43.108
much love, I'll see you soon.

00:13:49.243 --> 00:13:52.187
- And you know, Pat Riley and Dale Brown

00:13:52.187 --> 00:13:53.139
are similar guys.

00:13:53.139 --> 00:13:55.259
They teach you to never give up.

00:13:55.259 --> 00:13:57.459
You know, I can remember a game,

00:13:57.459 --> 00:14:00.779
we weren't playing well
and Pat Riley comes in,

00:14:00.779 --> 00:14:02.811
"You guys mind aren't in it."

00:14:02.811 --> 00:14:05.963
And he comes in with
a big bucket of water.

00:14:05.963 --> 00:14:07.443
It's all up here.

00:14:07.443 --> 00:14:08.595
You can do anything you want.

00:14:08.595 --> 00:14:11.139
I going to put my head in
that bucket for three minutes.

00:14:11.139 --> 00:14:12.971
And everybody sitting
there, like yeah, the record

00:14:12.971 --> 00:14:14.443
is a minute and 30.

00:14:14.443 --> 00:14:15.631
Like people that go scuba diving,

00:14:15.631 --> 00:14:17.059
a minute and 30 maybe two.

00:14:17.059 --> 00:14:18.075
And he did it for three minutes.

00:14:18.075 --> 00:14:18.908
- [Interviewer] Oh, come on.

00:14:18.908 --> 00:14:20.144
- Three minutes, Ernie.

00:14:20.144 --> 00:14:23.291
He stuck his head, ask
him next time you see him.

00:14:23.291 --> 00:14:24.964
- With his hair under there?

00:14:24.964 --> 00:14:25.797
He got his hair under there too?

00:14:25.797 --> 00:14:26.827
- Yes.

00:14:26.827 --> 00:14:28.011
- I don't know which part
of that is more amazing.

00:14:28.011 --> 00:14:29.235
- I'm telling you, he did it.

00:14:29.235 --> 00:14:32.723
So the guys are looking at
it like, "You know what,

00:14:32.723 --> 00:14:33.619
"he's right."

00:14:33.619 --> 00:14:36.369
So, his speeches and his stories.

00:14:37.283 --> 00:14:38.955
I always tell people,

00:14:38.955 --> 00:14:41.234
that's what always took
me to the next level.

00:14:41.234 --> 00:14:42.594
Not training, not going out

00:14:42.594 --> 00:14:44.371
and being in the gym three hours,

00:14:44.371 --> 00:14:46.179
conversation.

00:14:46.179 --> 00:14:49.701
- So those kind of
things, whether it's Sarge

00:14:49.701 --> 00:14:53.618
or whether it's Dale
Brown or Phil and his Zen,

00:14:54.891 --> 00:14:58.091
or Pat Riley, those
were the kind of things

00:14:58.091 --> 00:15:01.424
that gave you that umph that you needed?

00:15:02.811 --> 00:15:07.219
- Yes, because growing up,
it took a disciplinarian

00:15:07.219 --> 00:15:08.755
to make me what I am.

00:15:08.755 --> 00:15:12.675
It took a disciplinarian for
me to stop being a follower

00:15:12.675 --> 00:15:13.660
and learn to be a leader.

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:16.706
I was a medium level juvenile delinquent.

00:15:16.706 --> 00:15:18.371
I used to come home and get in trouble.

00:15:18.371 --> 00:15:22.090
My father would just say,
"That's how being a follower man.

00:15:22.090 --> 00:15:23.723
"I know your friends
wanted to steal the car

00:15:23.723 --> 00:15:24.556
"and you jumped in the car with them.

00:15:24.556 --> 00:15:26.622
"Now everybody's in trouble.

00:15:26.622 --> 00:15:28.824
"You got to stop that, you got
to learn how to be a leader."

00:15:28.824 --> 00:15:31.208
- Tell me this, do you feel any pressure

00:15:31.208 --> 00:15:33.737
because people say that now Shaq is in LA,

00:15:33.737 --> 00:15:35.944
we're going to win a
championship right away?

00:15:35.944 --> 00:15:37.088
I know that you probably came here

00:15:37.088 --> 00:15:38.061
to try and win a championship,

00:15:38.061 --> 00:15:39.880
but do you feel like all
the pressure is on you

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:41.164
to come and win one?

00:15:41.164 --> 00:15:43.208
- I really don't believe in pressure.

00:15:43.208 --> 00:15:46.322
My job is to just go out and play well.

00:15:46.322 --> 00:15:47.824
And you know, you have to realize that

00:15:47.824 --> 00:15:49.728
all the expectations they set on me,

00:15:49.728 --> 00:15:53.112
those are the same expectations
that I set for myself.

00:15:53.112 --> 00:15:54.648
I just want to come out here and win,

00:15:54.648 --> 00:15:58.920
Never give up, work hard,
and continue to learn.

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:02.224
Not only do I talk the talk,
I try and walk the walk.

00:16:02.224 --> 00:16:04.808
I left LSU in 1992, in 2000
I received my Bachelor's

00:16:04.808 --> 00:16:08.560
so my mom said she was going to whip me.

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:11.393
(loud applauding)

00:16:12.944 --> 00:16:14.737
Momma had an alter-ego too.

00:16:14.737 --> 00:16:16.520
And her name was Bigger Belt.

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:17.848
(audience laughing)

00:16:17.848 --> 00:16:20.819
In 2004, I received my MBA.

00:16:20.819 --> 00:16:24.504
(audience applauding)

00:16:24.504 --> 00:16:27.560
In 2012, I received my
Doctorate in Education.

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:30.727
(audience applauding)

